. Circuit Connections SummaryA. HC-SR04 Ultrasonic Sensor → ArduinoVCC → Arduino 5V  GND → Arduino GND  Trig → Arduino Digital Pin 9  Echo → Arduino Digital Pin 10  B. L298N Motor Driver → ArduinoIN1 → Arduino Digital Pin 2 (Left Motor Forward)  IN2 → Arduino Digital Pin 3 (Left Motor Reverse)  IN3 → Arduino Digital Pin 4 (Right Motor Forward)  IN4 → Arduino Digital Pin 5 (Right Motor Reverse)  ENA → Arduino Digital Pin 6 (Left Motor PWM Speed Control - remove jumper)  ENB → Arduino Digital Pin 11 (Right Motor PWM Speed Control - remove jumper)  C. L298N Motor Driver → MotorsOUT1 & OUT2 Terminals → Left DC MotorOUT3 & OUT4 Terminals → Right DC Motor(If a motor spins backward when it should move forward, swap its two terminal wires at OUT1/OUT2 or OUT3/OUT4)D. External Battery & Power DistributionBattery (+) Positive → L298N 12V Terminal  Battery (-) Negative → L298N GND Terminal  L298N GND Terminal → Arduino GND Pin (Crucial: Shared Ground Reference)  Arduino Powering Options:Option 1: Power Arduino via USB cable / separate 9V battery plugged into the DC jack.Option 2: If using a 7.4V–12V battery, connect Battery (+) to Arduino VIN and Battery (-) to Arduino GND.🔌 Quick Wiring MatrixFrom (Component)PinTo (Destination)PurposeHC-SR04VCCArduino 5VSensor Logic Power  GNDArduino GNDCommon Ground  TrigArduino Pin 9Trigger Pulse  EchoArduino Pin 10Distance Echo Return  L298N DriverIN1 / IN2Arduino Pins 2 / 3Direction (Left Motor)  IN3 / IN4Arduino Pins 4 / 5Direction (Right Motor)  ENA / ENBArduino Pins 6 / 11PWM Speed Adjust  Power SupplyBattery (+)L298N 12VMotor High-Current Power  Battery (-)L298N GND & Arduino GNDShared Common Ground Reference  
